=== REASONING ===

--- Why ADR-015 invariants are preserved ---

I1 default-off: The feature registry entry sets DefaultOn=false.
  features.CoverageOK passes. tools/aigen rewrote web/src/ai/features.ts
  with default_on=false in the mirror. No code path turns this on
  implicitly.

I3 baseline intact: RouteEfficiencyPage.tsx still imports/renders all
  pre-existing sections (summary stats grid, RouteCard list,
  comparison BarChart, MetricBar panels). The AI section is added
  ABOVE the comparison chart so the baseline content is still visible
  regardless of the gate's state, and the visible deterministic chart
  remains the canonical narrative. No baseline component was removed,
  reordered destructively, or wrapped in a gate.

I4 zero egress: All provider calls in the new strategy MUST flow
  through `internal/ai/dispatch` which composes the locked decorator
  chain (redaction → rate-limit → cost-cap → audit → trace). Tools
  read from the existing DriveRepo via a thin Source interface — no
  bespoke SQL, no direct provider import in feature code.

I5 hidden UI: AIRouteEfficiencySuggestions is wrapped by withAiFeature.
  Both halves of the gate are tested:
    - ai_mode='off' + toggle=true → empty container.
    - ai_mode='cloud' + toggle=false → empty container.
  The positive control (mode='cloud' + toggle=true) proves the gate is
  not permanently hidden by a typo.

I6 404 routes: ai_route_efficiency_handler_test.go's
  TestRouteEfficiencySuggestionsAIOffShowsMetricsOnly drives the
  guarded route via the real guard.Handler and asserts
  status == http.StatusNotFound when ai_mode='off'.

I7 per-feature opt-in: The toggle-off case in the React test +
  guard's per-feature lookup in the Go handler test prove that mode
  alone is not enough — the feature ID must also be enabled.

I10 type system: Registry entry was added to the canonical Go
  registry.go file; tools/aigen regenerated web/src/ai/features.ts
  from it (verified by --check exit 0 after regeneration). No drift.

I12 client/bg: This slice declares one background job
  ("ai_route_indexer") in registry metadata. The matching
  internal/jobs/ai_route_indexer.go is fail-closed (off-mode +
  toggle-off + settings-read-error all skip without fanning out). No
  push kinds. No client storage. The TS mirror's
  client.serviceWorkerChunks is "ai-route-efficiency-suggestions"
  which is a chunk-name reservation only; no actual service-worker
  code added in this slice. AI-OFF contract section below cites the
  matching tests.

--- Why the chosen design ---

1. routeID as opaque positive-int64 anchor.
   The baseline data is keyed on (start_place, end_place) — there is
   no stable primary key for a "route". The slice's REST path
   /routes/{routeID}/efficiency/suggest demands a numeric anchor, so
   I treat routeID as a positive int64 the LLM is told to use as
   context (the system prompt instructs the model to first call
   query_route_efficiency for the vehicle and use the anchor as a
   1-based index into the returned list). This keeps the URL shape
   future-compatible if a stable route_id is later introduced
   without changing handler signature semantics today.

2. Tools split: retrieve_route_chunks + query_route_efficiency.
   The retrieval tool requests source_types from the allowlist
   {drive_summary, route_efficiency, weather_context} but only
   drive_summary is wired in F7 today. The other two strings are
   forward-compat reservations matched by an allowlist check —
   no embedding SQL leaks into this slice. The read-only DB tool
   aggregates the same way as the deterministic baseline handler so
   the LLM and the chart agree on the figures it narrates.

3. Strategy is system-prompt-driven + tool-bound.
   The strategy file pins the FeatureID + system prompt + allowed
   tool list. Decorator wiring is implicit via internal/ai/dispatch.
   No provider adapter is imported here.

4. Eval coverage = 3 deterministic goldens.
   home_to_work_commute (positive, dominant commute);
   weekend_runs (positive, multi-trip variety);
   refusal_other_user (refusal — cross-tenant data smuggling).
   Each has a canned mock-provider response wired through F6 so
   `make ai-eval-fast` / `ai-eval -feature route-efficiency-suggestions`
   runs deterministically.

